course: dictionary
lesson: 11729
title: Averting: stopping or turning away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Averting means stopping something bad from happening, or turning something away. «The firefighters worked fast, averting a disaster at the factory.» The disaster did not happen because of their work.
explain: Averting can also mean turning your eyes or face away. «She kept averting her eyes from the scary film.» She looked away so she did not have to see the scary parts.
explain: Use the context clues to choose the meaning. If the sentence mentions something bad, like a disaster or a crisis, averting means stopping it. If it mentions eyes or a face, averting means turning away.
fact: Averting is the -ing form of the verb «avert».
fact: «Averting» means stopping something bad from happening, as in «averting a crisis».
fact: «Averting» can also mean turning your eyes or face away from something.
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning: «she kept stopping her eyes from the film» does not fit, but «she kept turning her eyes away from the film» does.
fact: A disaster is a sudden event that causes great harm, and a crisis is a time of great danger or trouble.
exercise: «The doctor worked quickly, averting a serious illness in the patient.» What does averting mean here? | Painting a picture | Singing a loud song | *Stopping something bad from happening | Turning a face away
exercise: «He kept averting his eyes from the spider.» What does averting mean here? | *Turning his eyes away | Counting the spider's legs | Catching the spider | Looking at the spider very closely
exercise: In «averting a crisis», which word is the bad thing being stopped? | a | *crisis | stopping | averting
test: «The lifeguard was quick, averting a tragedy at the pool.» What does averting mean? | Turning a face away | Swimming very fast | *Stopping something bad from happening | Splashing loudly
test: Why might a person be averting her face? | To make a loud noise | *To turn away from something she does not want to see | To show she is hungry | To stop a bad thing from happening in the town
exam: Which sentence uses averting to mean turning away? | «The nurse was averting the crisis at the hospital.» | «The bridge was averting a storm.» | «The team worked hard, averting a flood in the town.» | *«He kept averting his gaze from the blood.»
